WI-mifag (gate METHODS in the test-only-reachability ratchet) needs a
self-map in which a method reference resolves to its owning type. The
scip-python backend (WI-nanom) provides that, opt-in, and the cron's
map build never opted in.

.woodpecker/full-suite.yml self-tree-validation now:
- installs nodejs/npm (bookworm), @sourcegraph/scip-python@0.6.6 (the
  pinned fixture version) and hypergumbo-lang-scip-python;
- opts in for this step only via its environment
  (HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON=1, NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=9000:
  V8's default heap aborts at 4.2 GB on this tree);
- waits for test-all-packages and self-claims-gate (summed peak 10.3 GB
  measured locally; the CI VM has 16 GB, owner 2026-10-20) and runs on
  their failure too (when: status [success, failure]), so a red suite
  does not skip both ratchets;
- runs the reachability gate with --require-pass scip_python: both of
  the backend's preconditions fail silently into the plain map, so a
  map the pass did not contribute to exits 1.

Measured on dev (after WI-nijod #1746 and INV-pijij), whole tree:
plain map 5m32s / 3.9 GB, backend map 8m47s / 10.3 GB summed; the
scip_python pass emitted 55,281 nodes; Python method calls typed 9,435
of 9,619 (98.1%; 0 on the plain map). Per consumer of the shared map:
check-self-tree-validation matrix {} (exit 0, no re-baseline);
reachability gated cohort 293 keys, identical to the baseline (no
re-freeze: functions do not move; methods are WI-mifag's).

